**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** Every location the app reads gets one Domain shape and one set of defaults (001 §G 'Locations', 'Every path is overridable'; 001 §C 'Settings'; .spec-md §3.9, §5 `DataLocations`). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs`, module `WorkbenchSettings`, after the `WorkbenchSettings` record (`WorkbenchSettings.fs:87-101`), opening `Softellect.Sys.Primitives` for `ConnectionString` and `FolderName`, the types `AppSettingsProvider` reads and `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate` takes (step 62): the record `DataLocations = { libraryConnection : ConnectionString; backupsFolder : FolderName; preferencesFolder : FolderName; kitsFolder : FolderName; exportsFolder : FolderName; cataloguesFolder : FolderName; shippedCatalogueFolder : FolderName }`. Its doc is one to three lines: every location of 001 §G, each an `appsettings.json` key read once at the composition root (spec 0050 S2.4). Each field has a one-line doc: the library database's SQLite connection string; its `Backups` folder; the per-user preferences folder; the suggested parent of kit folders; the exports folder; the catalogue-export folder; the shipped catalogue. (a) `static member shippedCatalogueDefault : FolderName` is `FolderName "Catalogue"`, the shipped catalogue as a folder relative to the install folder (001 §G '`<install>\Catalogue\`'). (b) `static member defaultsUnder (documents : FolderName) : DataLocations` answers the 001 §G defaults as configured text, environment variables unexpanded, `documents` being the user's Documents folder the composition root passes: `libraryConnection` = `ConnectionString "Data Source=%LOCALAPPDATA%/Softellect/Berreman/OpticalConstructor/library.db"`; `backupsFolder` = `FolderName "%LOCALAPPDATA%/Softellect/Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Backups"` (001 §G: `Backups\` beside the database); `preferencesFolder` = `FolderName "%APPDATA%/Softellect/Berreman/OpticalConstructor"`; `kitsFolder`, `exportsFolder` and `cataloguesFolder` = `Optical Constructor/Kits`, `Optical Constructor/Exports` and `Optical Constructor/Catalogues` under `documents` through `FolderName.combine`; `shippedCatalogueFolder` = `shippedCatalogueDefault`. This is the one place the default texts are written. It reads no environment and touches no disk. `WorkbenchSettings` and `WorkbenchSettings.defaults` are unchanged, so nothing that builds settings reaches a location by default (.spec-md §3.9). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs`, on the `type CatalogueProxy with` extension that holds `createBuiltIn` (step 38): `static member createBuiltInUnder (shipped : FolderName) : CatalogueProxy` answers `CatalogueProxy.create` over `shipped`'s `Builtin` subfolder, the one place the `Builtin` name is written. `createBuiltIn ()` becomes `createBuiltInUnder` of `DataLocations.shippedCatalogueDefault` under `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory`, so its own `Path.Combine` is deleted and the shipped folder's name has one home. Each doc is one line citing spec 0050 S2.4. No environment expansion, existence check, cache or fallback folder is added: resolving configured text is AppConfig's (step 82). (3) Tests. `WorkbenchSettingsTests` gains `DataLocations.defaultsUnder holds the 001 §G locations as configured text`: over `FolderName "D:/Docs"` (test-local text, never a real folder), every field of `DataLocations.defaultsUnder` equals the text above, the three Documents folders being `FolderName.combine`d under it, and `shippedCatalogueFolder` is `DataLocations.shippedCatalogueDefault`. `CatalogueFolderTests` gains `createBuiltInUnder reads the Builtin catalogue of the shipped-catalogue folder it is given`: `createBuiltInUnder` over `Catalogue` under `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory` reads `Ok` the same catalogue as `CatalogueProxy.create` over `Catalogue/Builtin` there, the path spelled out in the fact, and over a fresh empty folder under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, "CatalogueFolderTests")` answers `CatalogueIoErr`.

**Acceptance.** After the locations land, `WorkbenchSettings.fs` MUST declare `DataLocations` with `defaultsUnder` and `shippedCatalogueDefault`, and `CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn` MUST read through `createBuiltInUnder`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `DataLocations.defaultsUnder holds the 001 §G locations as configured text` and `createBuiltInUnder reads the Builtin catalogue of the shipped-catalogue folder it is given`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s11 invariants MUST pass.
